              "President Donald Trump may hold talks with his Chinese counterpart Xi Jinping at a meeting of the Group of 20 nations at the end of next month to resolve the escalating trade dispute, a senior White House adviser said",
              "“Better to talk than not talk, but the talks have to be serious,” White House National Economic Council Director Larry Kudlow told Bloomberg Television in an interview Friday. G-20 leaders will meet in Buenos Aires from Nov. 30 to Dec. 1",
              "{\"author\":[{\"name\":\"Andrew Mayeda\"},{\"name\":\"Sarah Foster\"}],\"dateCreated\":\"2018-10-05T15:08:13.063Z\",\"dateModified\":\"2018-10-05T15:08:13.062Z\",\"datePublished\":\"2018-10-05T15:08:13.063Z\",\"description\":\"“Better to talk than not talk, but the talks have to be serious.”\",\"headline\":\"Trump May Meet Xi at G-20 Summit to Discuss Trade, Kudlow Says\",\"video\":{\"name\":\"Trump May Meet Xi at G-20 Summit to Discuss Trade, Kudlow Says\",\"description\":\"“Better to talk than not talk, but the talks have to be serious.”\\n\\n\",\"uploadDate\":\"2018-10-05T15:08:13.063Z\",\"duration\":\"PT3M3S\",\"contentURL\":\"https://www.bloomberg.com/media-manifest/videos/android/WiFi/23fbf519-c19f-483d-8f47-118f9d70ae03.m3u8?idType=BMMP\",\"transcript\":\"EXAMPLES OF WHY MANUFACTURING HAS TO BE DOMESTIC? I LARRY: OUR POLICY, THE PRESIDENT ' S TRADE POLICY HAS PUT THE CHINESE ON NOTICE THAT WE CANNOT ACCEPT THEIR UNFAIR TRADING PRACTICES, THEFT OF IP, FORCED TECHNOLOGY TRANSFER, HIGH TARIFFS ON INDUSTRIAL AND AGRICULTURAL COMMODITIES. THEY WON ' T LET AMERICAN COMPANIES OWN 51%. SOMETIMES THEY WILL SAY WE WILL GIVE YOU OWNERSHIP, BUT WE WON ' T GIVE YOU LICENSE. WHAT GOOD DOES THAT DO? THE PRESIDENT HAS BEEN ON GUARD. HE BELIEVES THE WHOLE TRADING RELATIONSHIP IS BROKEN. WE HAVE BEEN NEGOTIATING. IT HAS BEEN UNSATISFACTORY SO FAR. I THINK SECRETARY MNUCHIN HAS SAID BETTER TO TALK THEM NOT TALK. MAYBE, I WANT TO UNDERSCORE MAYBE, THERE MIGHT BE A MEETING BETWEEN THE PRESIDENTS AT THE G20 IN ONE IS AREAS -- BUENOS AIRES. THAT IS A MAYBE. I CANNOT CONFIRM THAT. WE HAVE DONE WELL ON THE USMCA. I HOPE I GOT THAT RIGHT. I HAVE TO LEARN THAT NEW PHRASE. WE ARE OPENING TRADE DISCUSSIONS WITH EUROPE, WITH JAPAN. THAT SENDS A SIGNAL TO CHINA. WE SIGNED THE TRIPARTITE, EU, USA, JAPAN AGAINST UNFAIR TRADING PRACTICES AIMED AT CHINA. THE WESTERN ALLIES ARE UNITED. SO FAR WE HAVE NOT GOTTEN ANY RESULTS FROM CHINA. JONATHAN: YOU CANNOT TEASE ME LIKE THAT WITH A MEETING IN BUENOS AIRES. ARE YOU HAVING TALKS ABOUT SETTING THAT UP AT THE MOMENT? LARRY: I ' M SORRY, I MISSED THAT. JONATHAN: ARE YOU HAVING TALKS RIGHT NOW ABOUT SETTING UP A MEETING BETWEEN THE LEADERS BETWEEN CHINA AND THE U.S.? LARRY: THERE IS DISCUSSION ABOUT THAT. I CANNOT CONFIRM IT. THERE IS DISCUSSION. BEFORE THEN, I DON ' T THINK SO, I DON ' T HEAR. I THINK IT IS BETTER TO TALK THEM TO NOT TALK, BUT TALK HAS TO BE SERIOUS AND SIGNIFICANT. NO SMOKE BLOWN. COME WITH CONCRETE PROPOSALS. SAY YES TO SOMETHING WE HAVE OFFERED. THE RELATIONSHIP HAS TO CHANGE. THE PRESIDENT WANTS TO PROTECT AMERICAN WORKERS, FARMERS, THE WHOLE ECONOMY. WE WANT A LEVEL PLAYING FIELD. IF THEY OPEN THEIR BARRIERS, WE WILL EXPORT, SELL A MILLION GOODS AND SERVICES. WE ARE THE HOTTEST ECONOMY IN THE WORLD. IF CHINA WANTS TO HELP ITS CONSUMERS, LET AMERICANS SUPPLY OUR SUPERIOR GOODS. WE HAVE NOT HAD ANY SATISFACTION ON THAT YET. JONATHAN: GREAT TO CATCH UP WITH\"},\"mentions\":[{\"name\":\"Politics\"}],\"publisher\":{\"name\":\"Bloomberg\"},\"hasPart\":{\"isAccessibleForFree\":\"False\"}}"
